VendorPulse Production Notes — kalpeshproduction
=================================================
Last updated: 2026-06-11

─────────────────────────────────────────────────
WHAT THIS COVERS
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
How to set up and deploy VendorPulse to production,
including the monitoring check org-reassignment feature
and the Docker .env fix.


─────────────────────────────────────────────────
ARCHITECTURE SUMMARY
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Laravel API       → Docker container (app)      → port 8000 (or APP_PORT)
- Horizon workers   → Docker container (horizon)
- Scheduler         → Docker container (scheduler)
- PostgreSQL        → Docker container (postgres)  → host port 54321 (prod may differ)
- Redis             → Docker container (redis)     → host port 63791
- Next.js dashboard → runs outside Docker (npm run start or PM2)

Local dev:  php artisan serve hits DB at 127.0.0.1:54321 (from .env)
Docker:     containers hit DB at postgres:5432     (from .env.docker)

KEY LESSON: Docker containers must use .env.docker (postgres:5432),
            NOT the local .env (127.0.0.1:54321).
            The docker-compose.bind.yml mounts .env.docker as .env inside containers.


─────────────────────────────────────────────────
FIRST-TIME PRODUCTION SERVER SETUP (run once)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. SSH into production server.

2. Clone / pull the repo:
     cd /var/www/vendorpulse
     git pull origin kalpesh

3. Copy the env template and fill in all secrets:
     cp deploy/liveproduction.env.template .env
     nano .env
     # Fill in: APP_KEY, DB_PASSWORD, MAIL_*, REDIS_PASSWORD (if any), APP_URL, etc.

4. Run the one-time setup script:
     bash vpproduction.sh setup
   This will:
     - Create .env.docker with DB_HOST=postgres, DB_PORT=5432, REDIS_HOST=redis
     - Add .env.docker to .gitignore so secrets are never committed

5. Run the first deploy:
     bash vpproduction.sh deploy
   This will:
     - Rebuild Docker images
     - Restart all containers (app, horizon, scheduler)
     - Run php artisan migrate --force
     - Run php artisan optimize (caches config using .env.docker = correct Docker hosts)
  - Install Playwright Chromium inside Docker runtime (required for Experience Monitoring)
  - Restart horizon/scheduler so workers pick latest env + browser cache

6. Verify everything is healthy:
     bash vpproduction.sh verify
   This checks:
     - DB connection from inside container
     - User and monitoring check counts
     - Latest monitoring log
     - Horizon status
     - Failed queue jobs


─────────────────────────────────────────────────
EVERY FUTURE DEPLOY
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

On your local machine — push code:
  git add . && git commit -m "feat: ..." && git push origin kalpesh
  cd web_dashboard && git add . && git commit -m "..." && git push origin kalpesh

On production server:
  cd /var/www/vendorpulse
  git pull origin kalpesh
  bash vpproduction.sh deploy
  bash vpproduction.sh verify

OR use the existing full deploy script:
  bash deploy/release.sh deploy


─────────────────────────────────────────────────
MONITORING CHECK ORG REASSIGNMENT (new feature)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

Frontend (super admin only):
  1. Go to Monitoring page.
  2. On any check row → three-dot menu → "Reassign organization".
  3. Select target organization.
  4. Click Preview (shows how many logs will move — dry-run, no changes).
  5. Type the check name to confirm.
  6. Click Execute move (runs in one DB transaction).

Backend Artisan command (direct / for scripts):
  Dry-run:
    php artisan monitoring:reassign-check CHECK_UUID FROM_ORG_UUID TO_ORG_UUID

  Execute:
    php artisan monitoring:reassign-check CHECK_UUID FROM_ORG_UUID TO_ORG_UUID --execute

  Inside Docker on production:
    docker exec vendorpulse-app-1 php artisan monitoring:reassign-check \
      cff63d39-888b-40fb-be8b-9b3d2563cf1c \
      84060050-6be8-4cce-98d9-7ae80afd42ad \
      7b4fb4cc-282b-4d87-ac44-daa0769ebf50

  What it moves in one transaction:
    - monitoring_checks.organization_id
    - monitoring_logs.organization_id  (all logs for that check)
    - domain_social_accounts.organization_id (if any)

  Safety checks built in:
    - Validates both orgs exist
    - Confirms check belongs to source org
    - Blocks if vendor ownership would be inconsistent
    - Blocks if related data already has mismatches
    - Default is DRY-RUN — must pass --execute to apply


─────────────────────────────────────────────────
KNOWN ISSUES AND FIXES APPLIED
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

Issue:  Docker containers read local .env (DB_HOST=127.0.0.1, port=54321)
        which doesn't exist inside the Docker network → connection refused.
Fix:    .env.docker created with DB_HOST=postgres, DB_PORT=5432.
        docker-compose.bind.yml mounts .env.docker as .env inside containers.
Files:  docker-compose.bind.yml, .env.docker (gitignored)

Issue:  Docker build failed due to root-owned screenshot files in storage/.
Fix:    .dockerignore now excludes storage/app/private/experience-monitoring/screenshots.
File:   .dockerignore

Issue:  Route not found for /api/v1/monitoring-checks/{id}/reassign
Cause:  Old Docker image (no bind mount) was serving requests without new code.
Fix:    Switched to docker-compose.bind.yml so container always uses live code.

Issue:  Experience Monitoring started failing with
  "browserType.launch: Executable doesn't exist .../.playwright-browsers/..."
Cause:  Playwright browsers were not present in the worker runtime after rebuild/restart.
Fix:    Install Chromium in runtime and keep only Docker workers active:
    docker compose exec horizon npx playwright install chromium
    docker compose exec app npx playwright install chromium
  Avoid running host `php artisan horizon`/`schedule:work` while Docker workers are up.


─────────────────────────────────────────────────
USEFUL COMMANDS ON PRODUCTION
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Check running containers
docker ps

# View app logs (live)
docker logs -f vendorpulse-app-1

# Clear caches inside container
docker exec vendorpulse-app-1 php artisan optimize:clear

# Run migrations
docker exec vendorpulse-app-1 php artisan migrate --force

# Check Horizon
docker exec vendorpulse-horizon-1 php artisan horizon:status

# Check failed jobs
docker exec vendorpulse-app-1 php artisan queue:failed

# Tail Laravel log
docker exec vendorpulse-app-1 tail -f storage/logs/laravel.log

# Check DB is reachable from container
docker exec vendorpulse-app-1 php artisan tinker \
  --execute='echo DB::connection()->getPdo() ? "DB OK" : "FAIL";'
